# Publish auth for the release workflow's `changeset publish` (.github/workflows/release.yml).
# changesets/action v2 (unlike v1) no longer auto-writes its own .npmrc from NPM_TOKEN --
# confirmed by grepping v2.1.0's real bundled dist/*.js (zero references to NPM_TOKEN or
# .npmrc anywhere) and by its own README, which points at Trusted Publishing (OIDC) instead
# and doesn't mention classic-token auth at all. Without this file, `npm publish` (inside
# `changeset publish`) fails with a real, confirmed error: `ENEEDAUTH: This command requires
# you to be logged in`, even with NPM_TOKEN correctly set as an env var -- npm never
# associates an env var with a registry on its own; something has to write this mapping.
#
# Harmless locally where NPM_TOKEN is unset (pnpm prints a non-fatal WARN on every command,
# confirmed not to block install/typecheck/test/check) -- only resolves for real in CI,
# where the workflow already sets NPM_TOKEN from the repo secret.
//registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken=${NPM_TOKEN}
